FINDING | program: shortwin-math | function: withdraw_in | bug_class: carry-crosses-empty-pool | group_key: shortwin-math | withdraw_in | carry-crosses-empty-pool
file: crates/shortwin-math/src/pool.rs:1908
status: Known finding independently reverified in pass 2; no new root cause.
root_cause: The last withdrawal sets total_shares to zero but retains the old holders' carry and carry_r for the next share supply.
description: A new lender receives the former lenders' undistributed SOL because the last withdrawal retains both credit remainders.
path: An existing lender deposits a large raw-token balance, receives a vested SOL credit, then withdraws all shares; a new lender deposits one raw token after the required sweep, receives one further SOL credit, and claims the inherited remainders.
proof: All inputs below fit their actual types: amounts and SOL use u64; shares, carry_r and acc_r use u128; acc and carry use i128. Set WAD=10^18, VA=1 and VS=1000, as pool.rs:73-78. An ordinary eligible SPL mint can have at least 2,000,000,000,000,000,000 raw units plus its venue reserves; mint_filter.rs:65-100 checks ownership, initialization, native-mint exclusion, freeze authority and extensions, with no supply ceiling below u64::MAX. Deposit T=2,000,000,000,000,000,000 raw units into an otherwise empty pool: shares_for_tokens at pool.rs:1720-1726 mints S=T*1000=2,000,000,000,000,000,000,000 shares. This ratio is the initial 1000 shares per raw unit, below R_MAX=1,000,000. No borrowed tokens or locks are required.
proof: An existing 1000-lamport lump can enter through sweep_trader.rs:266-283,301-310,359-370 and pool::sweep at pool.rs:2200-2225. It is actual vault SOL, not an unfunded rent receivable. Once its vest completes, release_in at pool.rs:898-928 credits it. credit_pos at 1033-1040 and credit_r_in at 1125-1134 compute floor(1000*10^18/S)=0 and remainder 1000*10^18=1,000,000,000,000,000,000,000 for each accumulator. Thus acc=acc_r=0, carry=carry_r=10^21, lender_sol=1000, vest_bal=0.
proof: The old lender withdraws all S with min_tokens=T and min_sol=0. tokens_for_shares returns floor(S*(T+1)/(S+1000))=T exactly. allowance allows T because borrowed_q=0 and no shares are locked. The existing handler's LastSharesBorrowed guard at instructions/withdraw.rs:205-209 passes because borrowed_q=0. withdraw_in at pool.rs:1906-1915 leaves S=0,T=0 and clears wipe_swept, but it does not change either carry. The old lender accrues zero because acc=acc_r=0; claim at pool.rs:2119-2129 pays zero. The vault still tracks and holds the 1000 lamports.
proof: Use a Raydium market without an old Pump UVA, so only the normal trader sweep bit is required. A zero-value sweep sets that bit even at S=0 (pool.rs:2191-2217) without consuming the retained carries. The new lender deposits amount=1,min_shares=1000: deposit.rs:109 permits it, the vest is empty, pool.rs:2008-2042 passes the sweep gate and mints 1000 shares. No open_short, minimum notional, borrowed position, stale price, keeper reward, or privileged action is needed. A further genuine one-lamport trader credit completes its vest. Both accumulators now increment by floor((10^18+10^21)/1000)=1,001,000,000,000,000,000. The new lender's 1000 shares accrue floor(1000*1,001,000,000,000,000,000/10^18)=1001 lamports. claim pays 1001, bounded by the actual lender_sol=1001. The old 1000-lamport remainder has crossed the empty pool into the new lender's allocation.
limits: This concrete trace transfers 1000 lamports, not the whole pool. A retained carry is below its previous share denominator, and its monetary magnitude is carry/WAD. No profitable repeated strategy or larger aggregate loss is established here. Raw-token supply and the timing of the last exit are explicit preconditions. The trace does not rely on a borrowed-token zero-share state, which the handler forbids.
fix: Clear both remainders when the last share burns, and account for them as dust under the existing epoch-roll policy.
fix_diff:
```diff
--- a/crates/shortwin-math/src/pool.rs
+++ b/crates/shortwin-math/src/pool.rs
@@ -1906,6 +1906,9 @@ fn withdraw_in(
     l.shares = sub_u128(l.shares, shares)?;
     p.total_shares = sub_u128(p.total_shares, shares)?;
     if p.total_shares == 0 {
+        p.dust = add_i128(add_i128(p.dust, p.carry)?, to_i128(p.carry_r)?)?;
+        p.carry = 0;
+        p.carry_r = 0;
         // AIR-08: the market has no lender again; SOL that reaches the trader from now on is
         // the protocol's (KI-10), so the next deposit waits for the sweeps, as after a wipe.
         p.wipe_swept = 0;
```
fix_limits: This mirrors the existing handling at pool.rs:2501-2503. It prevents the inherited allocation; it does not retrospectively pay fractional credits already rounded away.
funding_note: Each tiny trader donation and sweep can share one transaction; engine/trader.rs:139-183 checks a System-owned empty trader and transfers its entire balance to the rent-exempt market vault, leaving the trader at zero. The trace does not require a persistent under-rent account.
verification: Static source trace and integer arithmetic only; no build, test, program execution or runtime reproduction.

